00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.320
Because I'm gonna sock you, that's what for.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:43.150
Well, you wouldn't sock a guy with a stomach full of soda, would you?

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.490
I sure would.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:46.860
Yeah.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.050
Yeah, but don't forget, there's three of us.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.060
Uh-uh, I'm not fighting anybody.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.600
Me neither.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:16:57.130
Come on, Larry.

00:16:58.050 --> 00:16:59.970
I don't have to leave here if I don't want to.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.420
And if you start something, you'll get in big trouble with Mr. Peabody.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.440
All right, Larry. Now I know what you are.

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:10.850
You're a rat. That's what you are.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:15.330
And I'm never gonna speak to you as long as you live, because you're such a big rat.

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:17.370
Okay, beaver, okay.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:28.820
That. You're calling me, you know something, Larry?

00:17:29.710 --> 00:17:29.970
You...

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.350
kind of a rat.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.470
What's new on the Larry Beaver feud?

00:17:41.320 --> 00:17:43.400
Well, Larry called three times,

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.540
and the first two, Beaver managed

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.440
to be too busy, and the third time

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:49.600
he said he didn't know anyone named Larry Mondello.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.480
You know, Beaver has his point

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.620
this time. Larry should have paid that money back.

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:56.590
Dear, maybe I ought to call Mrs. Mondello.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:58.280
Oh, no, I don't think

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.400
I would if I were you.

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.460
Just leave the kids alone. They'll work it out somehow.

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:04.720
But if the parents try to arbitrate this thing,

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:06.480
they'll have to wind up enemies for life.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:12.200
Well, at least I'm sure Beaver doesn't have any real malicious feelings about Larry.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:12.940
Oh, no.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:26.130
This ought to fix him, huh, Walt?

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.130
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:29.970
But drawing...

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:31.840
and it isn't as good as really doing it to him.

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:34.370
Well, I wouldn't really do it to him,

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:36.680
but he deserves to have it drawn on him.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:38.620
What are you gonna do with this?

00:18:39.570 --> 00:18:42.110
Well, I was gonna send it to Larry to scare him,

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:44.330
but now I might save it till he's married

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:45.270
and send it to his wife.

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:48.530
You know you're not gonna do any of that junk,

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.170
don't you, Beef?

00:18:49.700 --> 00:18:51.670
Yeah, but it's good stuff to think about

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.280
because I didn't get to punch him.

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:02.310
How do you do, Mrs. Cleaver? Won't you come in?

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:06.600
Well, hello, Larry.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:08.680
How do you do, Mr. Cleaver?

00:19:09.090 --> 00:19:11.290
I would like to see the beaver, if you please.

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:12.650
Just a minute, Larry.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:14.380
Beaver!

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.460
Well, that's a nice parakeet.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:19.210
Does he talk, Larry?

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:20.980
Only to other birds.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:22.360
Beaver!

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:23.440
Yes?

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.130
You have company.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.470
Beaver, you come right down here.

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.580
Well, my sister named it Eagle,

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.280
so it shouldn't be scared of anything.

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:40.780
Oh, well, isn't that clever?

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:48.680
Well, Beaver, Larry's here.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.280
I know he's here.

00:19:57.400 --> 00:19:59.900
Well, don't you want to take him up in your room?

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:01.290
No.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.890
Can I speak to you alone in private, Beaver?

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.030
What for?

00:20:06.650 --> 00:20:09.510
Now, Beaver, Larry came all the way over here to see you.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:11.310
At least you can be nice enough to talk to him.

00:20:12.340 --> 00:20:13.700
Yes, sir, if you're gonna mate me.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:15.920
Yes, well, well.

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:16.900
Outside, fellas.

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:18.780
There you go.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:23.320
Ward, do you think you ought to go out there with them?

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:24.930
Well, June, please.

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:31.270
What's all this junk?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.040
Well, this is Eagle.

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:46.220
And in here are all my good Emmys, my best army men, and my empty CO2 cartridges.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.470
And this is my Uncle Sam bank that I can't get open.

00:20:50.950 --> 00:20:53.000
Gee, how can we move over here?

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:56.450
Giving them to you on account I'm going away.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:58.680
Where are you going?

00:20:58.780 --> 00:20:59.700
To your grandmother's again?

00:21:00.060 --> 00:21:01.340
I'm going to Africa.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:02.450
Oh.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:06.460
I'm going to Africa to join the French Foreign Legion.

00:21:07.380 --> 00:21:09.300
They don't let kids in the French Foreign Legion.

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:13.640
Well, I'm not going to tell them I'm a kid.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:17.820
I'm going to go out on the desert and get killed.

00:21:18.410 --> 00:21:22.150
A lot of people that were mean to me and call me a rat are going to be sorry.

00:21:22.870 --> 00:21:25.170
No, Colin? Did your mother and father give me permission?

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:26.800
I'm not going to ask them.

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:29.980
I'm sneaking away tonight and ching-hying myself on a...

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:33.700
And when my mother and father find out, they're gonna cry.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.320
Your father's gonna cry?

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:39.260
Well...

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:41.440
Well, my mother and sister might.

00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:42.900
Well, so long, Larry.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:44.960
Yeah, so long, Beaver.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:49.380
You take good care of all my stuff.

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:50.200
Sure.

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:55.300
You know something, Beaver?

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:56.440
What, Larry?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:59.600
I wouldn't go and get killed on the desert.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.350
If you promise to be my friend again.

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:06.940
Yeah, I guess I could.

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:08.890
Gee, that's neat, Beaver.

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:10.530
Could I have my stuff back now?

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.850
But how about my 75 cents?

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:16.100
Yeah, sure.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.740
My father said I should give it to you.

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:20.800
Thanks, Larry.

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:22.130
That's okay.

00:22:22.710 --> 00:22:24.810
Hey, you wanna go over to my house and mess around?

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:26.730
Yeah, I guess we could.

00:22:26.890 --> 00:22:27.630
I'll go tell my mother.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:29.940
Okay, I'll wait.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:31.620
Yes, anoint should steal my junk.

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:33.320
Mom! Hey, Dad!

00:22:37.090 --> 00:22:37.690
Yes, Beaver?

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:41.000
Can I go over and mess around, and could I stay for lunch?

00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:45.090
Has Mrs. Mandela asked you?

00:22:45.780 --> 00:22:46.140
No.

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:48.640
He's gonna make her.

00:22:48.780 --> 00:22:56.800
He said he'd never speak to Larry again for the rest of his life.

00:22:57.370 --> 00:22:59.970
Dear, when you're Beaver's age, the rest of your life is seldom...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:16.820
than a few hours I got in the foreign legion gonna go right out doesn't get shot and die

00:23:16.820 --> 00:23:26.340
and everybody was gonna be sorry ah go on beef you didn't believe that junk did you no but figured

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:28.680
he must like me a whole lot to make up a story like that

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.280
What are you doing?

00:23:34.570 --> 00:23:35.130
Sit-ups.

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:37.550
Hey.

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:39.500
They're push-ups.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:40.920
Only you do them sitting down.

00:23:42.040 --> 00:23:47.150
Hey, Beeve, did you ever get your 75 cents back?

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:49.040
Yeah, Larry paid it back.

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:52.740
Well, now, what are you gonna do if he comes around next week

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:54.460
and ask you for a whole couple of bucks?

00:23:54.830 --> 00:23:55.930
Are you gonna give it to him?

00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:57.060
No.

00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.970
I don't think we got enough friendship for a whole two...

00:24:00.800 --> 00:24:03.200
we hardly had enough for 75 cents

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:04.600
yeah

00:24:30.960 --> 00:24:31.400
Thank you.
